% composition-bridge: Listen for how jazz-pop balances a clear song with elastic phrasing, piano conversation, dynamic arcs and room for musicians to answer one another.
% composition-context: Laila Biali is a Canadian singer, pianist, composer and broadcaster whose work moves between contemporary jazz and song-based pop writing.
% composition-distance: Original 3/4 C-major melody, words and delayed entry; no melody, lyric, piano voicing, solo or arrangement from "Satellite" is used.
% improv: {"id":"A","bars":"5-6","role":"solo voice or instrument","prompt":"Answer the three-note question","choices":["same contour","reverse contour","one repeated pitch"],"replyBars":2}
% improv: {"id":"B","bars":"9-12","role":"second group","prompt":"Choose the texture of the return","choices":["unison","enter two bars late","hum long notes underneath"],"replyBars":4}
% dossier-function: original Grade 3 jazz-pop listening bridge; students sing an ABA streetlight song, improvise a constrained two-bar answer and choose unison, imitation or held-tone texture for the final A
% dossier-elements: twelve bars in 3/4; C-major pitches C-D-E-F-G-A-B-C, C4-C5 range; quarters, eighth pairs, dotted-quarter/eighth figures, half notes and quarter rests; dynamic arch in B; ABA form 4+4+4; optional two-bar delayed imitation on the last A
% dossier-practice: Rehearsal key C; written range C4-C5. Dotted half = 58 target. Count three evenly before trying a gentle long-short eighth interpretation as a comparison, not a rule. Teach A, teach B, make one three-note answer, then add the selected final texture.
% dossier-accompaniment: Newly authored C-Am-Dm-G jazz-pop shell chords, one chord per bar; piano may play roots and sevenths while bass plays beat 1 and a brush marks all three beats. No transcription of Biali's piano language.
% dossier-lyrics: Original English lyric. The final four bars may be sung on words, "doo," or hummed when the chosen texture would make text unclear.
% dossier-honesty: AI-assisted original composition, 11 November 2026; not a jazz standard, not traditional and not by or in the style of Laila Biali. The label names the listening lens, not an authenticity claim.
% dossier-licence: CC0 1.0 for the tune, words, chords and ABC; the reference remains copyrighted.
% dossier-respect: Credit Biali's multiple roles and listen to her actual phrasing before discussing jazz-pop. Do not teach "swing" as a single universal jazz rhythm; compare straight and long-short readings and ask what changes.
% dossier-review: Grade 3 teacher, jazz educator, second score reader and student singing trial; all reviews still required
