N:HOW READ (2026-11-11): Every bar totals six eighth units. A bars 1-4: C quarter D eighth-E eighth G quarter; E dotted quarter D eighth C quarter; D-E eighths F quarter E quarter; C half plus quarter rest. B bars 5-8 rise from E4 to C5 and return. Bars 9-12 restate A with a changed final bar. Pitch range C4-C5, largest leap a fourth, ABA 4+4+4.
N:UNCERTAIN: The optional long-short eighths, delayed entry, vocal peak C5 and constrained improvisation need classroom testing. A jazz educator and second reader must review the framing and originality.
